            warranty, by BarBend's and Garage Gym Reviews' figures. But BarBend also gives its footprint as
            71 inches long and its weight as 212 lb, which is full-size by any measure. If you have
            room for 71 inches, our main <a href="/best-elliptical-machines-for-home/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">elliptical guide</a> covers SOLE's range.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Schwinn 430 and ProForm Carbon EL.</strong> The 430 showed as out of stock on Schwinn's
            store on 19 October and is 70.1 inches long by Schwinn's figure. Garage Gym Reviews includes the
            ProForm Carbon EL in its compact list, but gives it as 67.3 inches long, which is not much of a
            saving.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>NordicTrack X16.</strong> A 58.5-inch footprint with an auto-adjusting stride up to 32
            inches, and Garage Gym Reviews' pick for an adjustable compact elliptical. It is sold through
            NordicTrack rather than Amazon and depends on a paid <a href="/is-ifit-worth-it/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>iFIT subscription</a> for most of its features;
            it is carded on our main elliptical guide.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Sunny Health &amp; Fitness.</strong> Sunny's SF-E3912, Garage Gym Reviews' budget
            compact pick, showed as unavailable in both versions on Sunny's store. Sunny's Smart Compact
            Magnetic Elliptical (SF-E905SMART) was in stock at $299.99, and Sunny lists it at 40.7 by 26.4
            inches with eight magnetic levels and a three-year frame warranty, but we found no independent
